From 3c464195d7ea4cc463787d251e74663306884195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:31:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 153/157] XD Netplay v1.7.4: the host picks the format in the
 room; new Doubles OU format; Orre Colosseum is the default

The host changes the room's format with Change Format... next to Music &
Location (desktop) or Change Format in the battle setup section (Android).
Every player sees "Format: <name>", late joiners included; the server sends
it in a new XdFormat message and announces each change in chat. The change
is refused while a battle starts or runs, and it is checked against the
teams in the room: the host gets one line for their own or spare team, and
a seated opponent whose team breaks the new format is told to submit a new
one. The public room list keeps the tag the room opened with.

Opening a room no longer blocks on the format: the host sees one advisory
line instead, and Start is where legality is enforced, with a one-line
reason. Start also puts the format key back on the room's format, so a
launcher pick made while hosting cannot change what boots.

New format Doubles OU (id 8, tag "[DOU] "): Smogon ADV Doubles OU. Double
battle, Lv 100, all six battle (stock entry mode). Species Clause; Evasion
and OHKO Clauses as move bans (Double Team, Minimize, Fissure, Guillotine,
Horn Drill, Sheer Cold); Self-Destruct and Explosion banned; Mewtwo, Mew,
Lugia, Ho-Oh, Latias, Latios, Kyogre, Groudon, Rayquaza, Deoxys and Ninjask
banned; items unrestricted. The pinned rules record turns the in-game Item,
Sleep, Freeze and Self-KO clauses off and keeps Species on. It does not use
the $XD OU Fixes code.

One format list for every picker on both platforms, from shared core:
Orre Colosseum, OU, Doubles OU, Orre Unlimited, Orre Limited, Hoenn
Stadium, Hoenn Unlimited, Hoenn Limited, Multi (id 9, hidden until
MultiEnabled is on; not built yet, behaves as Free), Free. Android's
FormatBridge now takes the list, names, tags and rules from shared core.
Users who never picked a format now default to Orre Colosseum; a saved
choice, Free included, is kept.
